## Context
In the 14-day scan, 85 of 813 Skill calls failed; 74 say "No such tool available: Skill" (a subagent without the tool), and 15 Grep calls failed because Grep is absent in some sessions (`docs/2026-10-21-velocity-friction-scan.md`). The agent finds out at run time and retries by another route.

Either the profile that needs the tool carries it, or the brief tells the delegate what it lacks. Estimate: 1 author-hour, about 90% chance of removing these errors.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each profile in `profiles/` that instructs a Skill or Grep call has the tool, or its brief names the substitute
- [ ] A test or lint fails when a profile text calls a tool its definition lacks
- [ ] Scan over a later window shows the two error classes near zero
